WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.440
Qin Shi Huang's procession set out in grand style, banners fluttering — a truly magnificent scene.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:14.318
But one day, the emperor suddenly fell ill in his carriage, and his attendants were terrified.

00:00:14.668 --> 00:00:19.060
The attendants gathered around the carriage, their faces full of worry.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.706
Zhao Gao glanced sideways, a cunning smile on his face.

00:00:24.056 --> 00:00:27.392
Li Si frowned deeply, full of hesitation.

00:00:27.742 --> 00:00:30.694
They decided to conceal the news of the emperor's death.

00:00:31.044 --> 00:00:36.300
They even used the emperor's great seal to stamp the false edict.

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:41.522
The young Huhai was pushed onto the throne, sweating with nerves.

00:00:41.872 --> 00:00:44.992
The officials knelt down before him, one after another.

00:00:45.342 --> 00:00:50.598
Dark clouds covered the sky, and the palace was shrouded in darkness.

00:00:50.948 --> 00:00:55.028
A great wind whipped the banners before the palace, and hearts were filled with unease.

00:00:55.378 --> 00:00:59.722
This coup became the turning point in the fall of the Qin dynasty.

